    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "We propose a close relationship between the orientations of cross-beds and the cross-bed package confined joints in the Jurassic aeolian Aztec Sandstone cropping out in the Valley of Fire State Park (NV) and Navajo Sandstone in Zion National Park (UT). The field data demonstrates that the orientation of cross- bed package confined joints is related to the orientation of cross-beds, suggesting that in addition to the distribution of compaction bands, cross-bed orientation and the associated anisotropy also exert a strong control on the formation, and orientation of the joints. These results may have important implications for fluid flow through aeolian sandstones in reservoirs and aquifers.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Deng, Shang and Aydin, Atilla. (2014). The Role of Cross-Bed Orientation and the Related Anisotropy in the Distribution of Compaction Bands and Joints in Aeoliean Sandstone. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at: http://purl.stanford.edu/hz797cb1170",
